          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: embarcar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "embarcar — \"to board; to embark\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Los pasajeros ya pueden embarcar. Passengers can now board."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Used for planes as well as ships."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "embarcar is built on barca \"boat\", which is inherited from Late Latin barca (EtymDB). Getting on a plane is still getting on a boat."
            }
          ]
        },
